# Feature: YAMNet classifier + AudioSet folders

## How YAMNet treats long audio (use this in-app)

YAMNet is **not** a single-vector-for-the-whole-file model. After 16 kHz mono resampling it:

1. STFT (25 ms window, 10 ms hop) → 64-bin mel spectrogram.
2. Cuts **0.96 s patches** (96 mel frames) with **0.48 s hop** (50% overlap).
3. Each patch → 521 AudioSet sigmoid scores.
4. Output `scores` has shape **`(N, 521)`**, one row per patch. First patch needs ~0.975 s of audio.

Official inference averages those rows for a clip-level top-5. Per-frame scores can also show events that change over time (the “score-o-gram”).

**Application policy:** always run this framing on the full analysis waveform. For RAM, feed ~60 s chunks of 16 kHz audio with 0.96 s overlap and **concatenate frame scores**. Do not bypass classification for files > 60 s.

Constants (must match YAMNet, not our invention):

- `PATCH_WINDOW_SECONDS = 0.96`
- `PATCH_HOP_SECONDS = 0.48`
- `NUM_CLASSES = 521`
- `SAMPLE_RATE = 16000`

## Classifier (`python/core/classifier.py`)

- Load `https://tfhub.dev/google/yamnet/1` once in `YamnetClassifier.load()`.
- Class names from the model’s AudioSet CSV (not a user list).
- `frame_scores(waveform) -> np.ndarray` shape `(N, 521)`.
- `clip_scores(frame_scores) -> dict[str, float]` = mean over axis 0 (YAMNet’s usual clip aggregate).
- Input is always 1-D float32 16 kHz mono.

## Folders = class names

- Destination folder = filesystem-safe AudioSet class name (`sanitize_class_folder` — replace `/` and other illegal chars).
- `mkdir` that folder **the first time** a file is sorted there. Do not pre-create all 521 folders.
- Manual moves may target `Mixed` or any official (sanitized) class name.

## Mapping (`python/core/mapper.py`)

Pass **clip-level class scores** into `decide_destination`:

- `matching` = class names with score ≥ threshold (these become tags, including Silence).
- 0 matching → dest `Mixed`.
- else dest = **top foreground class** (sanitized). Silence / room tone / generic noise do not win the folder when any non-background class is ≥ threshold. Close scores among overlapping labels (Pour vs Water) do **not** create Mixed.

`destination_from_frames` mean-pools **non-Silence patches** for the folder decision. Tags use the max of full-file mean and that foreground mean so sparse events still tag and Silence can still tag.

`temporal_mix` → Mixed only if two or more **unrelated foreground** classes each win a substantial fraction of frames (e.g. ≥ 20% of the non-Silence patches). Ignore Silence / room tone / generic noise patches. Pour then Trickle is related. Water then Speech is not.

Relatedness: AudioSet parent/child (ignoring the 7 top-level roots as the only shared ancestor) plus Water↔Liquid so nature-water and pour/trickle stay one family.

No `yamnetToFolderMap`. No custom Wind/Noise/Voices buckets.

## Tags vs folder

One destination folder. Tags = **all** matching AudioSet class names. Write them even when dest is `Mixed`.
